---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — WhatMedia"
  description="WhatMedia privacy policy: 100% local in-browser processing, zero trackers, absolute privacy by design."
  lang="en"
  currentPath="/en/privacy"
>
  <div class="py-12 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-wm-muted">
        <a href="/en/" class="hover:text-wm-ink">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-wm-signal font-semibold">Privacy</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="mt-4 font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-wm-ink sm:text-4xl">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-wm-muted">
        Last updated: November 9, 2026 · GDPR & International Privacy Standards Compliant
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-wm-ink">
        <section class="rounded-xl border border-wm-ok/30 bg-wm-ok-light/30 p-6">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-wm-ok">
            Core Foundation: Local Processing by Default
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-wm-muted">
            WhatMedia was architected from day one under strict <strong>"Privacy by Design"</strong> guidelines.
            When using WhatMedia, media analysis and transcoding run entirely within your device's web
            browser memory. <strong>No media files are uploaded to our servers.</strong>
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold text-wm-ink">1. Personal Data Collected</h2>
          <p class="text-wm-muted">
            WhatMedia requires no account creation, no usernames, no email addresses, no phone
            numbers, and no passwords. We use zero tracking cookies, zero marketing tags, and zero
            browser fingerprinting scripts.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold text-wm-ink">
            2. Exceptional Case: Fallback Server
          </h2>
          <p class="text-wm-muted">
            If your mobile device hardware cannot handle in-browser encoding (missing modern
            codecs), WhatMedia may offer a temporary cloud processing fallback.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-wm-muted">
            <li>
              This option strictly requires your <strong>explicit consent</strong> via a dedicated confirmation
              modal.
            </li>
            <li>
              Files are processed using ephemeral cryptographically random tokens (256-bit UUID),
              stripping all non-essential metadata.
            </li>
            <li>
              Uploaded inputs and converted outputs are <strong
                >automatically deleted within 15 minutes</strong
              > maximum.
            </li>
            <li>Files are never shared, sold, or used for machine learning / AI model training.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold text-wm-ink">
            3. Self-Hosted Assets & Zero Third-Party CDNs
          </h2>
          <p class="text-wm-muted">
            To prevent IP address leakage to external corporations, all typography (Space Grotesk,
            Inter, JetBrains Mono) and scripts are self-hosted on our static hosting. No requests
            are ever made to Google Fonts or third-party content networks.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold text-wm-ink">4. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
          <p class="text-wm-muted">
            In compliance with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and international
            privacy laws, because we store no identifiable customer databases or account records, no
            profiling occurs. For security audits or inquiries, open an advisory on GitHub.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold text-wm-ink">5. Contact Information</h2>
          <p class="text-wm-muted">
            Security and privacy contact: <code>contact@nealix.org</code> or via <a
              href="https://github.com/rogerfarolix/whatmedia/security"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="text-wm-focus underline">GitHub Security Advisories</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
